 "note": [
  "Scripture source: the Indian Revised Version (IRV Hindi, CC BY-SA 4.0), fetched as USX from the ebible mirror (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/hin_irv/usx), all 66 books. Every mined span was sliced from that text by script, never typed. Each meditation opens with its John 15 verse; translators were told to use the IRV text of JHN 15:1-16 verbatim every time, so a verse reads identically wherever it recurs.",
  "Translated from the English as the fixture carries it, which already includes this slug's BODY_CORRECTIONS.",
  "Derived by measurement: a row is mined only when the translator reported the quotation verbatim AND the measurement confirms it (a 6+ character quoted segment of that block, or an 8+ character phrase in the chapter, is a byte substring of the cited IRV verse). adapted/self rows and 2 unconfirmed verbatim claims (John 15:1 ch19, Eph 3:19 ch20) are self_rendered. Unquoted echoes are not recorded.",
  "KJV/IRV divergences an editor should see: John 15:2 IRV छाँटता ('prunes') where Murray's English has 'cleanseth' — the verse is IRV, and Murray's own sentences render cleansing as शुद्ध करना so his argument that pruning is cleansing survives; John 15:1 IRV includes सच्ची where Murray quotes 'I am the vine'; Isa 27:2-3 'सुन्दर दाख की बारी' for 'a vineyard of red wine'; Phil 4:13 no 'Christ'; Heb 10:9 has no 'O God' in the IRV (ch23 builds 'I come to do thy will, O God' from Heb 10:7 fragments, recorded adapted); John 15:8 Murray reverses its halves, the IRV order is kept.",
  "Adapted quotations (IRV wording with person/grammar changed, recorded self_rendered): 2 Cor 4:10 adds प्रभु as the KJV has it (ch07); Rev 3:17 I→we (ch06); Col 3:3 your→our (ch10); Ps 43:4 my→our (ch24); several John 15 fragments trimmed where Murray trims them.",
  "Conventions: curly quotation marks mirror the English per chapter; Christ referred to in the singular (वह/उसका, IRV style) throughout — two translators first used the honorific plural and switched to match the rest; the reader is addressed as तुम, Christ in prayer as तू; 'surrender' समर्पण, 'consecration' अर्पण; chapter titles pinned to IRV wording (the two 'The Vine' chapters carry their verse: दाखलता (यूहन्ना 15:1) / (यूहन्ना 15:5)).",
  "ENGLISH SOURCE items NOT repaired (the Hindi renders the evident sense or mirrors, as noted): ch08 'The Word of God's pruning knife' (probably 'The Word is God's pruning knife'; rendered as that); ch30 block 4 'Yea, Lord, but I chose You!' reads as contradicting the chapter — the Hindi uses Christ's IRV words परन्तु मैंने तुम्हें चुना है, so it reads as the reader repeating His words; check against Murray's original; ch20 'speaks plainly out of the Father' (odd, rendered cautiously); ch26 block 2 missing subject; ch16 stray capital 'The Whole place'; ch10 'rise and walk' paired with Acts 3 (the IRV Acts 3:6 has no 'rise', Matt 9:5 used)."
 ],
